# VENDOR-DOCS -- programs this port ships whose OWN upstream project wrote a
# man page beside the source, which the Lexicon never carried.  Read by
# hostbuild/extract-man.sh, which renders each with groff/nroff and stages the
# rendering; nothing here is COHERENT's text or ours -- it is MGR's, pico's or
# screen's own documentation, name and all.
#
# Every MGR client and MGR itself carry a troff page under mgr/src/clients/ or
# mgr/src/mgr/, and pico and screen carry one beside their own source.  The
# rendering is needed because /bin/man only cats an article to $PAGER and this
# distribution ships no nroff macro packages, so nothing on the machine could
# format one.
#
# One line per program: <name> <TAB> <path to the .1/.man, relative to the repository root>.
# Every path is checked on each run: extract-man.sh refuses a row that names a
# file which is not there, so a page cannot go missing from an image quietly.
